# SABOTAGE: P7-F1 impersonation-write audit (ADR-040 §6.6; persona-7 P7-F1, security · ESCALATE).
# Every mutation executed under a live Samen.Impersonation scope MUST emit an attributable
# `impersonation_write` aud_event (operator id, session id, tenant subject, action). The
# enforcement point is Samen.Audit.ImpersonationWrite (the in-transaction, fail-closed change,
# registered on: [:create, :update, :destroy]), which emits via the shared
# Samen.Audit.ImpersonationEmit.emit/4. This sabotage short-circuits that shared emission so an
# impersonated write produces NO audit row (the write still succeeds) — reproducing exactly the
# P7-F1 gap the walk found. The named RED tests MUST fail (they find no row), proving the
# audit-presence assertions are not tautologies. The CONTROLs (normal tenant writes) are
# unaffected — they never expected a row.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/impersonation_write_audit_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED (P7-F1): an impersonated UPDATE emits an attributable impersonation_write aud_event
# MUST_FAIL: RED (P7-F1): an impersonated CREATE is audited too (not just update)
# MUST_FAIL: RED (bulk): an impersonated bulk_create audits EVERY created row
# MUST_FAIL: RED (bulk): an impersonated bulk_update audits EVERY affected row
# MUST_FAIL: RED (destroy): an impersonated single-record :destroy AND :destroy_permanently each audit (in-transaction)
# MUST_FAIL: RED (bulk): an impersonated bulk_destroy audits EVERY destroyed row
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_emit.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_emit.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_emit.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/audit/impersonation_emit.ex
@@ -26,5 +26,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Audit.ImpersonationEmit do
   """
   @spec emit(module(), atom(), term(), map()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}
+  # SABOTAGE (P7-F1): short-circuit the audit emission — impersonated writes leave NO row.
+  def emit(_resource, _action_name, _record, _marker) when 1 == 1, do: :ok
   def emit(resource, action_name, record, marker) when is_map(marker) do
     repo = AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.repo(resource, :mutate)
     org_id = marker[:org_id] && to_string(marker[:org_id])
